  "body": "Hi, \r\n\r\nwe creating a lot of rooms with a python script.\r\nThis script (python) uses requests and talks to the matrix api to do that.\r\n\r\nWhile creating a room ( '/_matrix/client/v3/createRoom' ) its possible to set the powerlevels via 'power_level_content_override' in json payload  for that room and overwrite defaults like powerlevels for users etc.\r\n( This works as expected and documented)\r\n\r\nI got a hint in https://matrix.to/#/#synapse:matrix.org that its possible to that for existing rooms via https://spec.matrix.org/v1.5/client-server-api/#put_matrixclientv3roomsroomidstateeventtypestatekey\r\n\r\nMaybe i missunderstand something but if i implement that i always get a 404 back from server with following content:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<html>\r\n  <head><title>404 - No Such Resource</title></head>\r\n  <body>\r\n    <h1>No Such Resource</h1>\r\n    <p>No such child resource.</p>\r\n  </body>\r\n</html>\r\n```\r\n\r\nImplementation in python:\r\n```\r\napiurl_rooms_state = '{}/_matrix /client/v3/rooms/{}/state/m.room.power_levels/'.format(matrix_host,matrix_room['room_id'])\r\ndata = { \"invite\": 100 }\r\n\r\nmodify_room = requests.put(apiurl_rooms_state, headers=headers, data=data)\r\nprint(modify_room)\r\nprint(modify_room.content)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt would be create if documentation ca be a bit clearer to figure out how to use this ( sorry i´m no full time programmer)\r\n\r\nSome help would be great ( i´m shure that i´m just misunderstand the usage of this apicall)\r\n\r\nThanks in Advanced. \r\n\r\n",
